

In versioning (especially in npm, Node.js, and package.json), the caret (^) and tilde (~) symbols control which package versions can be installed automatically.

Suppose a package version is:

4.18.2

Here:

4 = Major version
18 = Minor version
2 = Patch version
Caret (^)

^4.18.2

It means:

Allow updates to the minor and patch versions.
Do not allow updates to the major version.

Examples:

Available version	Will npm install it?
4.18.3	✅ Yes
4.19.0	✅ Yes
4.20.5	✅ Yes
5.0.0	❌ No

Tilde (~)

~4.18.2

It means:

Allow updates only to the patch version.
Do not allow updates to the minor or major version.

Examples:

Available version	Will npm install it?
4.18.3	✅ Yes
4.18.5	✅ Yes
4.19.0	❌ No
5.0.0	❌ No

# Functional Components in React -> functional components are just a normal javascript function and it just return a react element i.e. some piece of jsx

# Component Composoition -> A component inside another component is called as component composition

# note -> u can write javascript inside jsx

# PROPS -> Known as properties , it is something that you can pass to a component ,suppose i want to pass data dynamically to some component so how we can do that i.e. we can pass it as a prop

AS functional components are just a normal javascript function similary props are just normal argument to a function

Passing a prop to a component is just like passing a argument to a function

--> Passing props to a component 

<RestaurantCard 
resname ="Meghana Foods"
cuisine ="Biryani ,North Indian, Asian"
/>  ->this is known AS passing props to the components -> resname and cuisine


//not using keys (not acceptable) <<<<< index as a key <<<<< unique id (best practice) <<

Note -> To export multiple things from a file we can't export it using default , because default can be used only once , so to do mi=ultiple exports we have to use named exports

